---
Title: About
Description: Meet Garib Tigranyan, Tech Lead and Senior .NET Developer.
DestinationPath: about/index.html
---

@{
    Layout = "/_Layout.cshtml";

    var root = (
        Context.Settings.GetString("SiteBasePath")
        ?? "/dev-blog-garib"
    ).TrimEnd('/');
}

<section class="container page-heading">
    <span class="eyebrow">
        <span class="pulse-dot"></span>
        BEHIND THE BLOG
    </span>

    <h1>
        Hi, I'm Garib<span class="accent-dot">.</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Tech Lead, Senior .NET Developer,
        and a lifelong student of software engineering.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="container about-layout section">

    <div class="article-content">

        <h2>Why I write</h2>

        <p>
            I work on the problems that show up
            after a feature ships: evolving architecture,
            operational reliability, security boundaries,
            and making complex systems easier to understand.
        </p>

        <p>
            This blog is a record of practical lessons,
            not a collection of perfect textbook examples.
            I care about trade-offs, evidence,
            maintainability, and helping other developers grow.
        </p>

        <h2>What you'll find here</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>ASP.NET Core and modern C# patterns</li>
            <li>Architecture decisions for real teams and products</li>
            <li>Cloud, observability, DevOps, and delivery</li>
            <li>Secure APIs, identity, and authorization</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Let's keep learning</h2>

        <p>
            For quick lessons, find me on
            <a href="https://www.youtube.com/%40GaribTigranyan"
               target="_blank"
               rel="noopener noreferrer">
                YouTube
            </a>.
            For deeper thinking and production examples,
            explore the
            <a href="@(root)/blog/">articles</a>.
        </p>

    </div>

    <aside class="about-aside">
        <span class="kicker">WORKING PRINCIPLES</span>

        <p>Clarity over cleverness.</p>
        <p>Security by design.</p>
        <p>Observability before guesswork.</p>
        <p>Trade-offs over dogma.</p>
    </aside>

</section>
